@KayIter #44517 covers `maxRetries: 0`: the policy stops on the first attempt, so a failed request isn't replayed. There was no test for it, there is now.

That's the only replay I can find on the chat path. `llm.ts` already calls the SDK with `maxRetries: 0` (only title generation passes 2) and `SessionRetry.policy()` is the one `Effect.retry` around it in the processor. I haven't gone through the outer session loop, so I'd only promise "no replay of a failed request", not more.

Funny that it's the opposite of what I wrote it for: quota windows want unbounded, you want zero. Same knob either way.
